		<p>
			I am a mathematics Honours student at the Australian National University, supervised by
			Brett Parker. I also learn a great deal from Yixuan Li and Bai-Ling Wang.
		</p>
		<p>
			I work in symplectic topology and mirror symmetry. Building on work of Bai, Pomerleano and
			Teleman, I apply Morava <i>K</i>-theory to the Kirwan kernel and prove the Tolman–Weitsman
			description of the kernel over the integers for smooth symplectic reductions of compact manifolds
			by tori (<a href="/research/">preprint</a>). In my
			<a href="/research/#honours-thesis">Honours thesis</a> I suggest that there should be a chromatic
			Kirwan theory, and now I am working towards a Morava <i>K</i>-theory version of Martin’s theorem
			relating <i>M</i>//<i>G</i> and <i>M</i>//<i>T</i>.
		</p>
		<p>
			I am also working on quantum GIT under the guidance of Bai-Ling Wang.
		</p>

		<h2>Research interests</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Chromatic methods in symplectic topology:</strong> Kirwan maps and their kernels in
				Morava <i>K</i>-theory.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Mirror symmetry:</strong> Teleman’s conjecture on Fukaya categories and Hamiltonian
				reduction.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Quantum cohomology:</strong> quantum Kirwan maps and Gromov–Witten invariants of
				quotients.
			</li>
		</ul>

